        "id": "ex-td-local-entropy-maximum-below-global",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "A local entropy maximum below a feasible global maximum",
        "statement": "Take two independent separated one-species systems $A$ and $B$ with material constitutions $c_A,c_B$ inside an isolated compound. Write $D_A:=D_{c_A}$ and $D_B:=D_{c_B}$ for their equilibrium domains; each is $(0,\\infty)^3$ in $(\\hat U_i,\\hat V_i,\\hat n_i)$, and each full domain is designated as an open single-phase chart. Fix positive $\\hat V_A,\\hat V_B,\\hat n_A,\\hat n_B$, total energy $U_A+U_B=1\\,\\mathrm J$, $s_*=1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, and toy entropies $S_A=2s_*\\hat U_A$, $S_B=s_*\\hat U_B$, using the same formulas on the distinct tagged constitutions $c_A^{(\\lambda)}$ and $c_B^{(\\lambda)}$ for every $\\lambda>0$. Admit every listed separated pair in $\\mathcal C_{AB}$ from [[post-td-bulk-additivity]], and permit internal energy transfer through thermal contact while keeping volumes and amounts fixed. Let\n\n$$\\phi(x)=((x,\\hat V_A,\\hat n_A),(1-x,\\hat V_B,\\hat n_B)),\\qquad \\mathcal F=\\{\\phi(x):x\\in(0,3/10]\\cup[3/5,9/10]\\}.$$\n\nThe retained barrier constraint admits exactly this nonconvex subset of the energy partitions; all its pairs satisfy the same total energy, volume, and amount constraints. The additive entropy is $S_{\\mathrm{tot}}(\\phi(x))=s_*(1+x)$, so $x=3/10$ is a local maximum relative to $\\mathcal F$ but lies below the feasible global maximum at $x=9/10$. These toy constitutive laws and constraints make no claim about a real material; calling an actual preparation metastable would require a separate kinetic model.",
